# Plain ESM .mjs scripts must check out with LF, unconditionally.
#
# BMPL-193(2): apps/api/test/run-integration.mjs is stored as LF in the repo
# (git blobs have always been LF-only here) but a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites it to CRLF. Vitest loads that file through
# Vite's SSR transform, which parses plain .mjs with Rollup's own JS/AST
# parser rather than esbuild (esbuild handles .ts fine either way) — and that
# parser mis-tokenizes this specific file once it is CRLF, reporting a bogus
# "Invalid or unexpected token" that points nowhere near any real problem.
# CI checks out LF by default and never sees it, so the break is invisible
# there and only bites a Windows contributor's local unit-test run. Pinning
# eol=lf makes every checkout of a .mjs file LF regardless of the checking-out
# machine's core.autocrlf, independent of anyone's personal git config.
*.mjs text eol=lf
